DDIFF(1)                       ZOAU Command Syntax                      DDIFF(1)

NAME

	ddiff - Compare two datasets (partitioned and sequential) matching one
	or more patterns

SYNOPSIS

	ddiff [-dhiv] [-Q <TMPHLQ>] [-c <COLS>] [-C <NUM>]
		  [<DATASET-PATTERN-1>] [<DATASET-PATTERN-2>]

	-c
		Specify column comparison specifiers to pass to SUPERCE.

	-C
		Display <NUM> lines of context around a displayed line.

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-i
		Ignore case.

	-Q
		Use an alternative high-level qualifier (HLQ) for temporary dataset
		name. This will override the TMPHLQ environment variable.

	-v
		Print verbose information.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

	TMPHLQ:	overrides the current high-level qualifier used for temporary
	dataset name.

DESCRIPTION

	Compare two datasets to each other. The datasets can be specified using
	standard wildcards and may be sequential, partitioned, or partitioned
	dataset members.

	ddiff supports generation dataset relative name
	notation when the name is fully specified with no wildcard characters.

	The -C and -i options behave in a manner consistent with diff.

EXAMPLES

	Compare 2 text files from columns 1 to 72:

		ddiff -c1:72 tstradm.data1.txt tstradm.data2.txt

EXIT VALUES

	0
		No differences between the files compared.

	1
		ddiff compared the files and found them to be different.

SEE ALSO

	diff(1)
